"""The service's exception family, one module per HTTP status.

| Module | Status | The question the refusal answers |
| --- | --- | --- |
| ``bad_request`` | 400 | the current state does not allow it |
| ``unauthorized`` | 401 | who are you? |
| ``forbidden`` | 403 | you are, and you still may not |
| ``not_found`` | 404 | this does not exist |
| ``conflict`` | 409 | this collides with what is already stored |

Every class subclasses the SDK exception of its status, so
``register_exception_handlers`` renders the envelope and
``error_responses(...)`` documents it in OpenAPI. Each one declares
``code``, ``message`` (a constant from
:mod:`src.core.constants.messages.errors`) and, when one input is the
culprit, ``field`` — **in the class body, with no ``__init__``**: what the
SDK reads without instantiating (``error_responses``, the
``BaseRepository``, ``tempest openapi-errors``) is then visible on the
class. Data that changes per raise goes in ``details=`` at the raise site:
``raise ItemNotFoundException(details={"item_id": item_id})``.

Import from this package, never from the status module:
``from src.core.exceptions import ItemNotFoundException``.
``tests/unit/core/test_exceptions_contract.py`` freezes the status,
``code``, message and ``field`` of every class re-exported here.
"""

from .not_found import ItemNotFoundException as ItemNotFoundException

__all__: list[str] = ["ItemNotFoundException"]
